# Woven fork — upstream baseline (read by scripts/woven-manifest-guard.sh)
#
# The upstream commit the fork was last merged from. Everything reachable from
# HEAD but absent here is fork divergence; the guard requires a manifest row for
# each such file that upstream ALSO owns.
#
# UPSTREAM_COMMIT is the authority, not UPSTREAM_TAG: upstream's tags are not
# pushed to this fork's origin, so `v0.27.4` does not resolve on a CI checkout.
# The commit does — it is the merge commit's second parent, so a full-history
# checkout (actions/checkout with fetch-depth: 0) always has it. The tag is
# recorded for humans.
#
# Update this in the SAME commit as the merge — see the merge-time checklist in
# scripts/woven-patch-manifest.md.

